{"id":"chatcmpl-315158b2-6213-4005-8ce3-5b938bcf1490","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229127,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a localization-then-verification workflow for determining laterality of a finding in a medical image. The key insight is that image-space position must be explicitly mapped to patient anatomy using orientation markers, rather than assumed. Verification against a known reference (side marker) is used to confirm the mapping before answering.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task asks 'which side' of an image a finding is on, first localize the finding in image coordinates, then separately map image-space to patient-space using orientation cues.\",\n    \"Use a dedicated grounding/localization tool to find the target structure before reasoning about its attributes (side, position, extent).\",\n    \"Insert an explicit verification step that checks the assumed coordinate-to-anatomy mapping against an independent orientation marker (e.g., 'L'/'R' labels) before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Distinguish image-left/right from patient-left/right explicitly in reasoning; never conflate them, since standard frontal imaging mirrors laterality.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging laterality tasks\": \"Localize the finding first, then resolve laterality via orientation markers or standard convention; verify the mapping before answering.\",\n    \"Spatial reasoning over annotated images\": \"Separate 'where in the pixel grid' from 'where in the real-world referent'; use explicit reference markers to bridge the two.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted visual QA\": \"Chain a grounding tool for localization with a verification step for interpretation; keep the two stages distinct.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding is localized (image coordinates known) before reasoning about its side or position.\",\n    \"Confirm the image-to-patient orientation mapping using an explicit marker or standard convention before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":470,"total_tokens":846,"completion_tokens":376,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":470},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":376}}}